# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Both are required — src/lib/supabase.ts throws
# without them rather than failing later with an opaque network error.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# The hCaptcha SITE key (public). It does three jobs:
#
#   1. the sign-in form requires a captcha when this is set (and Supabase Auth
#      must have hCaptcha enabled with the matching SECRET under Auth > Attack
#      Protection — a site key here with no secret there makes sign-in fail
#      rather than merely be unguarded);
#   2. the public feedback and comment forms are OFFERED ONLY WHEN THIS IS SET.
#      Their Edge Functions refuse a write with no captcha, so a form without
#      this could only throw away what somebody typed;
#   3. it must be paired with HCAPTCHA_SECRET as a Supabase function secret —
#      see the "public write path" section of supabase/README.md.
#
# Leave it blank and the site works, minus those forms.
VITE_HCAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
